            <ArticleTitle>Knowing About Device Algorithms to Understand the Rhythm and Role of Managed Ventricular Pacing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1179547617729651</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1179547617729651</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 66-year-old patient with a DR pacemaker for intermittent atrioventricular block presented with an electrocardiogram (ECG) showing some P waves non followed by QRS complexes, raising suspicion of device dysfunction. The device was equipped with a special algorithm (Managed Ventricular Pacing; Medtronic), and the observed ECG tracing was a normal consequence of the function of such algorithms. Being aware of the function of specific algorithms is essential to adequately analyze rhythms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
